litematica_upgraded.config.name.perfthreadedbuild=Build Schematic Chunks On Threads
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perfthreadedbuild=Chunks next to you are built on the background threads too, so standing inside a big placement does not stutter. Off: those chunks are built on the render thread, as stock Litematica does.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.perfbuildthreads=Build Threads
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perfbuildthreads=How many threads build the schematic chunks. 0 is automatic (your CPU count, limited by memory); 1 builds everything on the render thread.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.perfskipemptyslices=Skip Empty Slices
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perfskipemptyslices=A 16-high slice of a placement that holds no blocks is skipped when building instead of being walked cell by cell.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.perffastcopy=Fast Placement Copy
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perffastcopy=Copying a placement into a still empty schematic chunk skips the air cells instead of looking at each one.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.perfghostmove=Ghost Move
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perfghostmove=While you move a placement, its built chunks are drawn shifted without rebuilding; once it stays still the real rebuild runs in the background and replaces them.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.perfsparsestorage=Sparse Storage
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perfsparsestorage=Big, mostly empty schematics only use memory for the 16 x 16 x 16 sections that hold blocks, and a file that does not fit in memory gives an error message instead of a crash.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.perfshowstats=Show Speed Numbers In F3
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perfshowstats=Adds the build numbers (threads, queue, builds per second, render-thread build time, skipped slices) to the Litematica line of the F3 screen.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.perfbatchdraw=Batch Drawing
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perfbatchdraw=Built schematic pieces are grouped into bigger draw jobs, so the game makes far fewer draw calls each frame. The picture stays the same. Off by default: it saves no frame time on most PCs and can stutter while a schematic is being built.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.perflazytranslucentsort=Lazy See-Through Sorting
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perflazytranslucentsort=Glass, water and other see-through blocks are re-sorted only after you moved a real distance, not every frame.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.perfautoworkers=Leave A Core For The Game
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perfautoworkers=With Build Threads on 0 (automatic), uses your CPU cores minus one (at least one), so one core is always free for the game. Off: Litematica's own count.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.perffardetail=Less Detail Far Away
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perffardetail=Pieces far away are drawn without the outline lines. Switches itself off when the game is low on memory.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.perfmovefullcopy=Complete Copy While Moving
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perfmovefullcopy=While you move a placement, a complete copy of it is drawn (also the blocks that already match the world), so it shows no holes. It is kept until you deselect the placement, so the next move shows it at once.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.perffullcopybudgetmb=Complete Copy Memory (MB)
litematica_upgraded.config.comment.perffullcopybudgetmb=How much graphics memory the complete copy may use. 0 is automatic: a quarter of the free graphics memory, or 128 MB when the card cannot tell. Turn off Complete Copy While Moving to use none.
litematica_upgraded.config.name.displaylists=Display Lists (Use VBOs Off)
litematica_upgraded.message.perf.feature_off=Litematica Upgraded: "%s" did not work here and is off until you restart the game.
litematica_upgraded.message.perf.out_of_memory=This schematic does not fit in memory (Minecraft has %s MB). Give the game more RAM.

